{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "title": "Dependency resolution evidence",
  "$comment": "Written whether the resolution succeeded or was refused. A refusal that leaves no trace is indistinguishable from a step that never ran.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "runId",
    "stageId",
    "status",
    "blueprintSha256",
    "materialisations",
    "checks",
    "findings"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "runId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "stageId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
    "status": { "type": "string", "enum": ["completed", "blocked"] },
    "dryRun": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false,
      "$comment": "True when the stage rehearsed: every check that reads this run's own files was made, but no resolver was started and no lock file exists. A rehearsal that recorded an exit code would be claiming a resolver ran."
    },
    "blueprintSha256": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^$|^[0-9a-f]{64}$",
      "$comment": "Identifies the exact approved blueprint whose toolchain choice was honoured, so a later reader can tell which design this lock file belongs to. It hashes the raw bytes, not a canonical reading of them."
    },
    "materialisations": {
      "type": "array",
      "$comment": "One plan can ask for several lock files. A scalar record would describe only the last one and hide the rest.",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "recipe",
          "toolchainId",
          "toolchainSha256",
          "ecosystem",
          "registry",
          "manifestPath",
          "lockPath",
          "projectPaths"
        ],
        "properties": {
          "recipe": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "toolchainId": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "toolchainSha256": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^$|^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
          "ecosystem": { "type": "string" },
          "registry": { "type": "string" },
          "manifestPath": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "lockPath": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "projectPaths": {
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 }
          },
          "resolverExitCode": { "type": ["integer", "null"] },
          "durationSeconds": { "type": ["number", "null"] }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "checks": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["name", "outcome", "detail"],
        "properties": {
          "name": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1 },
          "outcome": { "type": "string", "enum": ["passed", "failed", "skipped"] },
          "detail": { "type": "string" }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
      }
    },
    "findings": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" } }
  },
  "allOf": [
    {
      "$comment": "A refusal can happen before the blueprint is even read, so the identifying fields are only knowable once resolution completed. Demanding them on every record would force a refusal to invent them.",
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "status": { "const": "completed" },
          "dryRun": { "not": { "const": true } }
        },
        "required": ["status"]
      },
      "then": {
        "properties": {
          "blueprintSha256": { "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
          "materialisations": {
            "items": {
              "required": ["resolverExitCode", "durationSeconds"],
              "properties": {
                "toolchainSha256": { "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
                "ecosystem": { "minLength": 1 },
                "registry": { "minLength": 1 },
                "resolverExitCode": { "type": "integer", "const": 0 }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "$comment": "A rehearsal that completed still identifies the blueprint and the toolchain it would have resolved against - those are read from files this run already wrote - but it must not report an exit code or a duration for a resolver that was never started. A rehearsal that was blocked may have refused before reading the blueprint at all, so it is held to the base constraints instead: requiring a digest of a file that was never opened would turn a controlled refusal into a validation failure.",
      "if": {
        "properties": {
          "dryRun": { "const": true },
          "status": { "const": "completed" }
        },
        "required": ["dryRun", "status"]
      },
      "then": {
        "properties": {
          "blueprintSha256": { "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
          "materialisations": {
            "items": {
              "properties": {
                "toolchainSha256": { "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$" },
                "ecosystem": { "minLength": 1 },
                "registry": { "minLength": 1 },
                "resolverExitCode": { "type": "null" },
                "durationSeconds": { "type": "null" }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
